{
  "_comment": "PodMotion agent CRIU-scoped seccomp profile (ADR-0039 SD-5, ADR-0148). Default-deny (SCMP_ACT_ERRNO, errno EPERM=1). Allows the CRIU checkpoint/restore syscall surface plus the Go runtime; denies privilege-escalation, kernel-image-load, keyring, NUMA-policy, perf, and io_uring syscalls outright (they fall through to the default ERRNO action). ptrace(2) is arg-filtered on index 0 (the request) to exactly the request values CRIU issues: PTRACE_SEIZE=0x4206(16902), PTRACE_INTERRUPT=0x4207(16903), PTRACE_DETACH=17, PTRACE_GETREGSET=0x4204(16900), PTRACE_SETREGSET=0x4205(16901). Injection-capable requests (PTRACE_ATTACH=16, PTRACE_POKETEXT=4, PTRACE_POKEDATA=5, PTRACE_POKEUSR=6) are intentionally omitted and denied by default. Meaningful only after privileged:true is dropped (SD-1). The new-mount-API syscalls (move_mount, open_tree, fsopen, fsmount, fsconfig, fspick) are allowed for CRIU 4.x kerndat init: kerndat.c:1129 issues move_mount to probe MOVE_MOUNT_SET_GROUP support; under default-deny these EPERM and abort kerndat. CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE (cap 40) must also be present on the agent for that probe (see daemonset.yaml). Validate against an actual CRIU strace before production.",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
